<td width="100%" valign="top" align="left" class="mob-ps-0" style="text-align: left; font-family: Chivo, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #223341; font-size: 16px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 24px; padding-bottom: 16px; padding-left: 20px; width: 100%;"> <p style="margin: 0px; text-align: left;"><span style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px;">For smaller merchants like UK Universities, compliance with PCI DSS can be a challenge. A proven approach to compliance is to work with compliant Third-Party Service Providers (TPSP).</span></p> <p style="margin: 0px; text-align: left;">‌<br /></p> <p style="margin: 0px; text-align: left;"><span style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px;">Our latest <a style="color: #223341;" href="https://www.flywire.com/resources/on-demand-webinar-top-tips-for-managing-third-party-service-providers?utm_source=marketo&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=q3clientnewsletter"><span style="color: #48b985;"><u>webinar</u></span></a> provides an overview and tips around the actions required by universities and TPSPs.</span></p> </td> 
